  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I : In &#39;Lassaigne&#39;s Test&#39;, when both nitrogen and sulphur are present in an organic compound, sodium thiocyanate is formed.</p><p>Statement II : If both nitrogen and sulphur are present in an organic compound, then the excess of sodium used in sodium fusion will decompose the sodium thiocyanate formed to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCN</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options a: given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VAnYk",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.",
